{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJYvHVSDUYWe3Cc4vKmf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The retry problem was that every save attempt called the identifier generator again, so a retry of a partly completed save could take another identifier from the source. The fix is a per-submission `SavePatientTransactionManager` that remembers generated values and completed identifier additions, so a retry reuses them. I could not identify the commit or ticket that made this change: my tools don't expose commit history, and the code has no ticket reference for it. The only ticket key in the registration app is `O3-5912`, on an unrelated address-hierarchy test.\n\nThe registration app lives in `openmrs-esm-patient-management` (there is no `openmrs-esm-patient-registration` repo in Falkon).\n\n**Why more than one identifier was used:** Before this change, each attempt at `savePatientFormOnline` called `generateIdentifier(selectedSource.uuid)` for every auto-generated identifier. A retry after a partial failure (the patient save or an identifier addition failed after generation) therefore requested a fresh value, and the earlier value was never used.\n\n**The fix, as the code now reads:**\n- `form-manager.ts` (lines 217–235): before generating, it checks `generatedIdentifiers[fieldName]`. If an earlier attempt generated a value from the same source, that value is reused. Otherwise it generates one and stores it.\n- `form-manager.ts` (lines 250–265): for an existing patient, an identifier addition that already succeeded is skipped on retry (`addedIdentifiers`). A failed addition is retried with the same value.\n- `form-manager.ts` (lines 425–440): the `GeneratedIdentifier` type and the `SavePatientTransactionManager` class holding `patientSaved`, `generatedIdentifiers` and `addedIdentifiers`. Its doc comment says it exists so a retry only repeats the work that failed.\n- `patient-registration.component.tsx` (line 63): the manager is held in a `useRef`, so it survives retries within one form session.\n- `patient-registration.test.tsx` (lines 681–714): retry state is kept for the same patient and reset when the route patient changes.\n\n**Tests that pin the behaviour** (`form-manager.test.ts`, lines 673–787): a new-patient retry reuses `10001V`; an existing-patient retry does not repeat a successful addition; a failed addition is retried with the same value; a changed source generates a new value.\n\nNothing in the repository was modified.\n\nEvidence, best first:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 217, \"endLine\": 235},\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 250, \"endLine\": 265},\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\", \"startLine\": 425, \"endLine\": 440},\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\", \"startLine\": 673, \"endLine\": 787},\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.component.tsx\", \"startLine\": 63, \"endLine\": 63},\n  {\"path\": \"packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/patient-registration.test.tsx\", \"startLine\": 681, \"endLine\": 714}\n]\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1302,"cache_read_input_tokens":24212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1302},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbd31fb2-d358-4226-8900-aaf5b7f87450","uuid":"d39cd867-3df8-4eea-b717-8c8fbd1f6a00","timestamp":"2